WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.400
- We are thrilled and
honored to be here tonight

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.040
to pay tribute to the great Mel Brooks,

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.075
a comedic genius, and a legend-

00:00:07.075 --> 00:00:10.500
(audience applauds)
Beyond compare.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.720
- He was, of course, a
big part of our lives,

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.510
long before we were ever a part of his.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:17.040
- Starting at age 11,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.250
I replayed the "2000 Year Old Man" daily.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.230
In fact, until I was about 14,

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:24.600
I slept with that record playing,

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.700
hoping to get subliminally funnier.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.920
- Ah, what happened at 14?

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.390
- I discovered pornography.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.000
- Of course.
(audience laughs)

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.960
- So when the opportunity arose

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.760
to actually work with Mel,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.330
bringing the musical version
of "The Producers" to Broadway,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.000
it was the realization
of a childhood dream.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.070
- Same for me, even
while it was happening,

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.040
we knew it was such an
extraordinary and unique experience,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.180
it could never be topped.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.230
So thank you, Mel, for that
once in a lifetime opportunity

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.050
to become Bialystock and Bloom,

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.599
a memory we will always cherish.

00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:05.599
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.930
- In all of his work,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.290
Mel has always let humor lead the way.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.990
He proved that if it was smart and funny,

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.490
you can joke about anything.

00:01:14.490 --> 00:01:16.950
- Which is why he's won
every award known to man,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.597
with the possible exception
of the Latin Grammy.

00:01:19.597 --> 00:01:21.480
(audience laughs)

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:24.397
Although, I hear he's working
on an album with Bad Bunny.

00:01:24.397 --> 00:01:25.650
(audience laughs)

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.680
- Now, Mel is the first to
make jokes about his age,

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.480
but we are not going to do that tonight.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.180
- No, no, we're not gonna do that.

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.190
Although.
(audience laughs)

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.380
I will just say that
it is quite remarkable

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:41.400
that Mel is actually older
than this organization,

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:44.373
the Academy of Motion
Picture Arts and Sciences.

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.800
- Well, that's actually,

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.859
Nathan, that's nothing.

00:01:47.859 --> 00:01:50.040
Mel is older than penicillin.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.630
- Is that true?
- Yeah.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:53.730
Yeah, he's older than the aerosol can.

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.830
- I had no idea.
- Yeah.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.480
Older than FM radio.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:58.980
- I think that's enough.

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:00.360
- He's older than polyester.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.179
- Poly, he's older than polyester?

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:04.020
- Yes, yes.
- Really?

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.003
Wow, that is old.

00:02:06.003 --> 00:02:06.836
(audience laughs)

00:02:06.836 --> 00:02:09.180
Anyway, throughout
Mel's incredible career-

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.310
- He's older, older than the minimum wage.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.020
- Well, now you're just making things up.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.120
- Nuh-uh, nuh-uh.
(audience laughs)

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.460
- Anyway, throughout
Mel's incredible career,

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:19.710
he has occasionally had his detractors,

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:21.840
who have accused him of vulgarity,

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.781
to which he famously
replied, "That's bullshit."

00:02:24.781 --> 00:02:26.880
(audience laughs)

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.830
- Mel, you're an institution,

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.230
and we are so proud to be here tonight

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.525
to see you officially institutionalized.

00:02:34.525 --> 00:02:36.184
(audience laughs)

00:02:36.184 --> 00:02:39.600
- And now, because it
just doesn't seem right

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.323
to honor Mel Brooks
without breaking into song.

00:02:42.323 --> 00:02:44.100
(gentle piano music)

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.840
